     $vER: Platinum, v1.96 HISTORY (15-Sep-96) by Dotoran of Frontiers!
============================================================================
- v1.96 -

    - Released: September 15, 1996
    - New Features:
        - The amigaguide version listing now includes WHICH filelisting you
          are viewing in the initial title bar, instead of just using the
          text "An AmigaGuide Formatted Filelisting for [bbsname]".
        - All filelists received inclusions of the creation date in more
          places than at the END of the different ECHO listings. (This was
          one reason I didn't know about the "not updating archived list"
          bug that was squashed below).

- v1.95b -

    - Released: September 14, 1996 (again, to Greg ONLY)
    - Bug Fixes:
        - Greg alerted me to these bugs, either directly, or through other
          comments he made during recent chat sessions:
            - The ARCHIVED versions of the lists were NOT being updated
              properly, because the archivers saw the archives already had
              a file with the same name, so it skipped adding it. I added
              into the code some checks for existence, followed by some
              calls to the DELETE() command.
            - If you had text buttons set up, yet had a particular list set
              NOT to USE any of them, you'd still see a BUTTONS screen in
              the guide files. This screen contained an EMPTY button which
              led to a nonexistent node and a Table of Contents button. I
              changed this to NOT INCLUDE a BUTTONS screen if you had them
              disabled in the config for this particular listing.
            - While fixing the above, I also discovered a similar problem
              if you had the Table of Contents disabled for a list, as there
              were still some buttons that LINKED to a CONTENTS node, which
              would be nonexistent if you had the TOC disabled. These buttons
              will now link to either a BUTTONS node(or in the event that a
              BUTTONS node isn't to be used, a link to the ECHO1 node).
    - New Feature(s):
        - While fixing the bugs above, I disabled the creation of all my
          "real" listings, then created a quick TEST list that only had 1
          dir listing in it. While running Platinum using these settings, I
          noticed that it still read through ALL directory listings, even
          though ONLY ONE directory listing would be used. Platinum will now
          check to see if a directory will be used in at least ONE of your
          defined lists, and if it's seen to NOT appear in ANY listing, it
          will be SKIPPED during the initial scan phase.

- v1.95a -

    - Released: September 14, 1996 (to King Arthur ONLY)
    - Bug Fix:
        - Greg(aka King Arthur) reported a bug where the AmigaGuide listings
          would not open properly when used on the 2.04/2.1 version OS. I
          had to dig up an OLD copy of the AmigaGuide library to find this
          one. (I had been using the 40.4 version AmigaGuide, which I had
          mistakenly thought WAS the 2.04/2.1 version). Anyways, after some
          slight modifications, fixed this bug.

- v1.95 -

    - Released: August 14, 1996
    - This version had it's config module and files completely revamped.
    - First release I actually felt confortable and proud to release.

- v1.00 -

    - First attempt at a file with powers similar to Mercury. This version
      had some SERIOUS bugs. Production was ceased due to major HD problems
      at this end.

